pas","n":"Tapas","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Spanish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Tapas are appetisers or snacks in Spanish cuisine. They can be combined to make a full meal and are served cold (such as mixed olives and cheese) or hot (such as chopitos, which are battered, fried baby squid; or patatas bravas, spicy potatoes). In some bars and restaurants in Spain and across the globe, tapas have evolved into sophisticated cuisine. In some Central American countries, such snacks are known as bocas. In parts of Mexico, similar dishes are called botanas."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tapas"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tapas"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","ref":"site/spainonafork-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Spanish cuisine","links":[["Andrajos","dish/andrajos"],["Ataula","dish/ataula"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"],["Churro","dish/churro"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Cuajada","dish/cuajada"],["El Quijote (restaurant)","dish/el-quijote-restaurant"],["El Willy","dish/el-willy"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Esquina Común","dish/esquina-comun"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Hojuela","dish/hojuela"],["Jamón","dish/jamon"],["Migas","dish/migas"],["Mojo (sauce)","dish/mojo-sauce"],["Ogasawara-Hakushaku-Tei","dish/ogasawara-hakushaku-tei"],["Patatas a lo pobre","dish/patatas-a-lo-pobre"],["Patatas bravas","dish/patatas-bravas"],["Picatostes","dish/picatostes"],["Pincho","dish/pincho"],["Pottage","dish/pottage"],["Salchichón","dish/salchichon"],["Salmore